WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.960
These are the exact same investment
projections, the numbers haven't changed,

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:06.200
the only difference is how they're shown.

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:08.800
My family calls me the compound growth
preacher.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:13.520
When I was 18 years old, I came across a
compound interest calculator, and

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:17.600
seeing what a few decades could do to
ordinary contributions absolutely blew

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:18.800
my mind.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.320
And quite frankly, I became a pretty
annoying 18 year old to know.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:25.560
I was constantly telling people you need
to start investing early.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:30.040
But eventually, I got more interested in
why those same numbers weren't nearly

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:31.580
as convincing to other people.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:35.180
And I started wondering whether part of
the problem is how we're representing

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:40.160
compound growth. I had an ambitious
research idea and absolutely no budget.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:43.960
So of course, the next logical step was
grad school.

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:49.400
During my master's in marketing and
behavioral science, I designed and ran a

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:53.940
six experiment program investigating how
the visual presentation of compound

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:58.560
growth projections can influence
consumers' perceptions of that growth and

00:00:58.560 --> 00:00:59.800
their investment motivation.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:05.200
I own the project from end to end, from
developing the theory, designing and

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:09.740
programming the studies, recruiting
participants, analyzing the data, and

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:11.040
writing up the final paper.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:15.240
And what I found is that graphs made
compound growth acceleration more

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:19.420
apparent, which increased consumers'
confidence in that growth and led to

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:20.680
higher contributions.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:24.820
Five experiments later, my family still
groans when the compound growth

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:28.860
soapbox comes out. But unfortunately for
them, I don't plan to stop anytime

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:32.520
soon. I want to keep turning this
obsession into things that I can build,

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:34.100
launch, and improve.

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:38.420
I've spent my entire investing life on the
client side of Wealthsimple, and

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:40.740
now I want to see what I can build from
the other side.

00:01:40.952 --> 00:01:41.652
Thank you.

